'''''Lotus argyrodes''''' is a plant species in the genus ''[[Lotus (genus)|Lotus]]'' [[Endemism|endemic]] to the [[Azores]] and [[Madeira]] Islands.<ref name=":0">{{Cite web |title=Lotus argyrodes R.P.Murray {{!}} Plants of the World Online {{!}} Kew Science |url=http://powo.science.kew.org/taxon/urn:lsid:ipni.org:names:503485-1 |access-date=2024-08-12 |website=Plants of the World Online |language=en}}</ref>

==Description==
This species is a [[subshrub]] with succulent leaves each with fine hairs. The flowers have a red wing and a yellow beak, looking swanlike, along with a preseadhead flower part. the leaves are oval when mature.<ref>{{Cite web |title=Occurrence Detail 4399882037 |url=https://www.gbif.org/occurrence/4399882037 |access-date=2024-08-12 |website=www.gbif.org |language=en}}</ref><ref name=":0" />

This species also has green hairless seed pods that stick upright off the old leaves.<ref>{{Cite web |title=Occurrence Detail 4137663705 |url=https://www.gbif.org/occurrence/4137663705 |access-date=2024-08-12 |website=www.gbif.org |language=en}}</ref>

==Conservation status==
This species is actually considered [[Least-concern species|Least Concern]] by the Kew database.<ref name=":0" />

